  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nA slowly approaching cold front brings showers and storms into \nsoutheast Ohio this evening, then precipitation coverage becomes \nmore widespread overnight and Thursday. A few strong storms \ncould materialize and produce some strong gusty winds this \nevening; however, severe potential is expected to lessen for \nThursday as cloud cover and earlier/ongoing activity are likely \nto limit instability.\n\nThe main concern with this event will be potential for flash \nflooding. While antecedent conditions have been fairly dry, \nexcessive rainfall from training storms may lead to localized\nflash flooding. Heavy downpours could also cause a few issues \nin urban or poor-drainage areas.\n\nPrecipitation coverage should gradually lessen as the front \nbegins to drift south Thursday night into Friday morning.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nChances of showers and storms remain present through the end of\nthe week as a front lingers nearby on Friday, and then a \nshortwave passes by on Saturday. Thereafter, the pattern is \nlikely to remain active as another boundary stalls to the north \nearly next week, and a potential system steers a cold front \ntowards the area around mid week. That being said, specifics on \ntiming and placement of these features for next week are still \nuncertain at this point.",
